From c6d531aa609f83496a8471d157ef32e62895bd4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 09:55:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(warmup): bound pre-profile memory before weight residency

Upstream base: d05da62e9ccdf8e342b15bf6785d83224cc165af.

Rationale: compile model-selected JIT registrations after construction but before checkpoint loading; stream B12X warmup discovery; allocate MXFP8 trial activations only while their individual plan is prepared; and reclaim accelerator scratch between plans. This prevents hundreds of serving-size preparation inputs and compiler transients from accumulating alongside resident DS4.1 weights.

Quality implications: none. Kernel selection, compile keys, prepared plans, checkpoint values, execution paths, and arithmetic are unchanged; only startup phase ordering and temporary-input lifetime change.

Tests: added active-registry/model-loader ordering, incremental B12X discovery, lazy MXFP8 trial allocation, and per-plan reclamation regressions. Python compilation, Ruff, formatting, and patch whitespace checks pass. The local environment lacks pytest and PyTorch, so target-image tests and guarded TP3 startup remain required.

Upstream status: local candidate for vLLM; intended for upstream review after GB10 qualification.
